From: JiaY-shi <shi05275@163.com>
Subject: [PATCH] net: ethernet: mtk_wed: fix HW RRO double free during SER

mtk_wed_free_rx_buffer() already releases the HW RRO buffer through
mtk_wed_hwrro_free_buffer().  Do not release it a second time from the
SER RX reset path, otherwise a Wi-Fi recovery can pass a stale page
pointer to __free_pages() and panic the kernel.

mtk_wed_hwrro_free_buffer() leaves dev->hw_rro.pages and .desc pointing
at the memory it just freed, so the second call walks a freed page list,
unmaps and frees each page again and hands the same coherent allocation
back twice.

Signed-off-by: JiaY-shi <shi05275@163.com>
[backport to 6.12, same code as 6.18]
Signed-off-by: Andrey Korshunov <razor1702@gmail.com>
---
--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/mediatek/mtk_wed.c
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/mediatek/mtk_wed.c
@@ -1746,7 +1746,6 @@ mtk_wed_rx_reset(struct mtk_wed_device *
 				   false);
 	}
 	mtk_wed_free_rx_buffer(dev);
-	mtk_wed_hwrro_free_buffer(dev);
 
 	return 0;
 }
